---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About — Krista Allison, DVM"
  description="Veterinarian with six years of clinical experience and a research background, moving into pharmacovigilance, drug safety, and medical affairs."
>
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl">About</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pb-16 grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_260px] gap-10">
    <div class="prose text-[--color-ink]">
      <p>
        I am a veterinarian with six years of clinical experience and a research
        background that came before it. I have worked across small animal, large
        animal, equine, and exotic medicine, in everything from a solo rural
        practice to a high-volume corporate hospital, and the thread through all
        of it has been the same: our patients deserve personalized care, and good
        science is how we get there.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before veterinary school I worked in neuroscience and cancer research,
        with peer-reviewed publications and formal research presentations along
        the way. In practice I have leaned on that background constantly, whether
        I am reading an unfamiliar ultrasound pattern, building a new anesthesia
        protocol for the team, or translating a complicated diagnosis into
        something an owner can actually act on. I like the teaching part as much
        as the medicine, and I have spent a lot of my career helping students,
        technicians, and support staff grow.
      </p>
      <p>
        Now I am moving that experience into industry. Clinical practice has
        shown me where drug safety, protocol design, and medical communication
        succeed and where they fall short, because I have watched it play out on
        real patients. I want to bring that point-of-care perspective to
        pharmacovigilance and medical affairs, where the decisions we make ripple
        out to thousands of animals we will never meet.
      </p>
      <p>
        I do not think there is a single right way to practice this profession.
        Private, corporate, academic, and industry all have a part to play, and
        the work I want to do sits at the seams between them.
      </p>

      <h2>What I bring</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Clinical decision-making and adverse-event recognition on live patients.</li>
        <li>Clinical research and study design; protocol development.</li>
        <li>Scientific and medical writing; translating complex science for any audience.</li>
        <li>Multi-species clinical expertise across small animal, large animal, equine, and exotic.</li>
        <li>Diagnostics: radiograph, ultrasound, and cytology interpretation.</li>
        <li>Staff training and education; cross-functional collaboration.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <aside class="text-sm">
      <img
        src="/krista.jpg"
        alt="Krista Allison, DVM, in a white coat holding a calico cat"
        width="260"
        height="325"
        class="rounded-xl border border-[--color-line] object-cover w-full"
      />
      <dl class="mt-6 space-y-4">
        <div>
          <dt class="text-[--color-ink-dim]">Education</dt>
          <dd class="text-[--color-ink]">DVM, Auburn University (2020)</dd>
          <dd class="text-[--color-ink]">BS Biology, University of Montevallo (2015)</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-[--color-ink-dim]">Focus</dt>
          <dd class="text-[--color-ink]">Pharmacovigilance, drug safety, medical affairs</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-[--color-ink-dim]">Certifications</dt>
          <dd class="text-[--color-ink]">Fear Free Certified; AVMA; AAIV</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-[--color-ink-dim]">Links</dt>
          <dd><a href="/cv">Curriculum vitae</a></dd>
          <dd><a href="/publications">Publications</a></dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </section>
</Layout>
